[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The Plan view: a collapsible tree over the declaring directories

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-PLAN-TREE
TITLE: The Plan view: a collapsible tree over the declaring directories
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The Plan view renders the canon as a collapsible tree with the selected
node's full card in the right pane, sharing one card renderer (card.js) with
the Graph view so a node reads the same in both. Groups are the declaring
directories; within a group a node nests under the same-group node it
Assumes (first parent wins, cycles fall back to flat), which is exactly the
edge the shared-understanding carve writes for its concept tiers. Selection
lives in the #hash like the Graph view; the shared-understanding group opens
by default. The Graph pill is labelled Graph, not Board, to stop the view
shadowing the app's name.
<<<
